# Regression: opening and closing the game menu must leave the top strip AND the scene
# pristine. QFG1 target, save slot 1 (room 300: the Game/Action dropdown extends deep into
# the scene over the green half-timbered Hero's Tale Inn at rows ~30..110).
#
# Two round-2 Roger defects this pins (both on the mouse-menu path):
#   #1 stuck menu-title strip — SCI closes the mouse menu via bitsRestore of the full menu
#      strip (reverting the NATIVE pixels to the score banner) with NO follow-up
#      kernelDrawStatus, so the enhanced strip stayed stuck on "File Game Action
#      Information" while native showed the banner (SBS-confirmed). After close the strip
#      must revert to "Quest for Glory I [score ...]": m-open (titles) must differ from
#      m-after over the strip band (presenceDiff), AND m-after must equal the pre-menu
#      banner m-before over the strip band (sameRunDiff). The banner text does not animate.
#   #2 scene-deep dropdown stamp — a closed dropdown must not leave a tracked non-enhanced
#      pixel stamp (priority-255, NOT healed by mouse-over) in the scene. The Game menu
#      dropdown covers the left Inn wall; after close + mouse-over that band must match the
#      pre-menu scene (m-before ~ m-afterhover over x[0..0.28] y[0.05..0.30] — the Inn wall,
#      left of the animating ego/NPC). A real stamp there is thousands of full-width px.
#
# NOTE: the SCI0 frozen mouse-menu loop does NOT observe injected MOUSEMOVE events, so a
# press-hold + `move` across titles does NOT switch dropdowns (it stays on the pressed
# title). Menus are opened one at a time with a real mousedown on the title x (verified:
# mousedown drops that menu open). Do NOT re-add vacuous drag `move` lines expecting a
# dropdown switch — they are dead coverage.
#
# `snap` (grabOverlay at execution time), NOT `capture` (pended, present-consumed): the
# composited cursor is parked off both checked bands (bottom-right) before each grab, and
# snap grabs AFTER the park move has been presented, so the boot-position arrow cannot land
# over the strip and inject cursor diff (the ~400 px flake that a pended capture caught).
wait 4000
move 300 185
wait 1000
snap m-before
# --- open the deep Game/Action dropdown over the left Inn wall, then close it ---
mousedown 100 2
wait 900
snap m-open
# release outside the dropdown to cancel-close (no menu item executed)
mouseup 260 150
wait 1400
move 300 185
wait 1000
snap m-after
# move the mouse THROUGH the dropdown's former scene footprint, then park off-band:
# a real stamp is priority-255 and is NOT healed by mouse-over, so it would still show.
move 40 34
wait 400
move 120 60
wait 400
move 300 185
wait 1000
snap m-afterhover
wait 300
quit
